  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis\n\n**Zero test infrastructure exists.** No test runner is wired up in either layer — `web/package.json` has no `test` script and no Vitest/Jest/Playwright dependency; `engine/pyproject.toml` lists `pytest>=8.3` as a dev dependency but there are no `test_*.py` files or `tests/` directory anywhere in the repo, and no `pytest.ini`/`[tool.pytest]` config. That's the top-level gap, ahead of any individual function.\n\nThe project is early — Phase 1/2 of the AGENTS.md build order. Almost every function in `engine/` is a `raise NotImplementedError(\"Phase N — ...\")` stub. That changes what \"coverage gap\" means here: for the engine, the actionable move is to write the tests **now**, against the stated contracts, so they drive the Phase 2/3 implementation (this matches AGENTS.md's own instruction to build the synthetic generator \"before the engine — you cannot develop a detector without knowing what it is supposed to detect\"). For `web/`, a handful of functions are real and testable today.\n\n---\n\n### 0. Infrastructure gap (do this first)\n\n- **web**: no Vitest/RTL. Add `vitest`, `@testing-library/react`, `jsdom` (or continue evaluating with Node's test runner for pure `lib/` functions only, if the team wants to defer React component testing). This needs your approval per AGENTS.md's \"ask before adding a dependency\" rule — flagging, not installing.\n- **engine**: `pytest` is already a dependency; nothing is configured. Add `tests/` with `conftest.py` fixtures for `CanonicalEntity`, `Match`, `Conflict`, `SurvivorshipRule` builders, and a `pytest.ini`/`pyproject.toml` `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` block (`testpaths = [\"tests\"]`).\n\n---\n\n### 1. `engine/pipeline/normalize.py` — untested, fully stubbed\n\n`fold_name` is the correctness-critical function in the whole normalization layer (AGENTS.md: folding must be \"deterministic and total\"). No tests exist for the suffix table, and it has real edge cases the current `LEGAL_SUFFIXES` tuple doesn't obviously handle (e.g. `\"Pvt Ltd\"` is listed as a single token but suffix-folding is usually word-by-word — worth deciding before implementing).\n\n```python\n# tests/pipeline/test_normalize.py\nimport pytest\nfrom pipeline.normalize import fold_name, normalize\nfrom connectors.base import RawRecord\n\nclass TestFoldName:\n    def test_case_insensitive(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"ACME INC\")\n\n    def test_strips_known_legal_suffix(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme\")\n\n    def test_collapses_whitespace(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme   Corp\") == fold_name(\"Acme Corp\")\n\n    def test_strips_punctuation(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme, Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme Inc\")\n\n    def test_multiword_suffix_pvt_ltd(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Pvt Ltd\") == fold_name(\"Acme\")\n\n    def test_deterministic_same_input_same_output(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme GmbH\") == fold_name(\"Acme GmbH\")\n\n    def test_empty_string(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"\") == \"\"\n\n    def test_name_that_is_only_a_suffix(self):\n        # edge case: \"Corp\" alone — must not fold to empty and crash downstream\n        assert fold_name(\"Corp\") != \"\"\n\n    def test_unicode_name(self):\n        fold_name(\"Société Générale\")  # must not raise\n\n    def test_suffix_as_substring_not_folded(self):\n        # \"Incoming Systems\" contains \"inc\" but is not the suffix \"Inc.\"\n        assert fold_name(\"Incoming Systems\") != fold_name(\"Incoming\")\n\n\nclass TestNormalize:\n    def test_original_name_preserved_alongside_folded(self):\n        records = [{\"Id\": \"001\", \"Name\": \"Acme Inc.\"}]\n        entities = normalize(records, entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\")\n        assert entities[0].name == \"Acme Inc.\"\n        assert entities[0].normalized_name == fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n\n    def test_missing_optional_fields_default_to_none(self):\n        records = [{\"Id\": \"001\", \"Name\": \"Acme\"}]\n        entities = normalize(records, entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\")\n        assert entities[0].parent_external_id is None\n        assert entities[0].last_modified_at is None\n\n    def test_empty_input_returns_empty_list(self):\n        assert normalize([], entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\") == []\n\n    def test_source_id_stamped_on_every_entity(self):\n        records = [{\"Id\": \"1\", \"Name\": \"A\"}, {\"Id\": \"2\", \"Name\": \"B\"}]\n        entities = normalize(records, entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-9\")\n        assert all(e.source_id == \"src-9\" for e in entities)\n\n    def test_malformed_record_missing_required_id_raises(self):\n        with pytest.raises((KeyError, ValueError)):\n            normalize([{\"Name\": \"No Id\"}], entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\")\n\n    def test_pure_function_no_side_effects(self):\n        # must not touch the DB or network — this is what makes it usable in eval/\n        records = [{\"Id\": \"1\", \"Name\": \"A\"}]\n        normalize(records, entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\")\n        # (assert via monkeypatched db.write_* raising if called, or via\n        # a static check that normalize.py imports nothing from db.py)\n```\n\n### 2. `engine/pipeline/blocking.py` — untested, fully stubbed\n\nThe AGENTS.md constraint that must be tested explicitly: **never O(n²)**. This is a performance correctness requirement, not just a functional one.\n\n```python\n# tests/pipeline/test_blocking.py\nfrom pipeline.blocking import block, score, combine, match, MIN_MATCH_CONFIDENCE\nfrom pipeline.schema import MatchSignals\n\nclass TestBlock:\n    def test_exact_key_pairs_returned_first(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(external_id=\"001\")\n        b = entity_factory(external_id=\"001\")\n        pairs = block([a], [b])\n        assert (a, b) in pairs\n\n    def test_no_candidates_for_disjoint_sets(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(external_id=\"001\", name=\"Zzz Unrelated\")\n        b = entity_factory(external_id=\"999\", name=\"Totally Different\")\n        pairs = block([a], [b])\n        assert (a, b) not in pairs or len(pairs) == 0  # depends on embedding threshold\n\n    def test_top_k_is_respected(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(external_id=\"1\")\n        many_b = [entity_factory(external_id=str(i)) for i in range(50)]\n        pairs = block([a], many_b, top_k=5)\n        assert len([p for p in pairs if p[0] == a]) <= 5\n\n    def test_does_not_compare_all_pairs(self, entity_factory, benchmark=None):\n        # regression guard for O(n^2): candidate count should scale ~ n*k, not n*m\n        side_a = [entity_factory(external_id=str(i)) for i in range(200)]\n        side_b = [entity_factory(external_id=str(i)) for i in range(200)]\n        pairs = block(side_a, side_b, top_k=10)\n        assert len(pairs) <= 200 * 10\n\n    def test_empty_sides_return_empty(self):\n        assert block([], []) == []\n\n\nclass TestScore:\n    def test_exact_key_match_scores_signal_true(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(external_id=\"001\")\n        b = entity_factory(external_id=\"001\")\n        assert score(a, b).exact_key is True\n\n    def test_identical_names_high_fuzzy_ratio(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(name=\"Acme Corp\")\n        b = entity_factory(name=\"Acme Corp\")\n        assert score(a, b).fuzzy_ratio > 0.95\n\n    def test_completely_different_names_low_signals(self, entity_factory):\n        a = entity_factory(name=\"Acme Corp\")\n        b = entity_factory(name=\"Zephyr Holdings\")\n        s = score(a, b)\n        assert s.fuzzy_ratio < 0.5 and s.exact_key is False\n\n\nclass TestCombine:\n    def test_combined_confidence_in_bounds(self):\n        s = MatchSignals(exact_key=True, cosine=0.9, fuzzy_ratio=0.9)\n        assert 0.0 <= combine(s) <= 1.0\n\n    def test