ise\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// web/types/source.test.ts — Zod schemas, currently unverified\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty objects array\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"filter is optional\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects a name over 80 chars\", () => { ... });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown kind\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"x\", kind: \"mysql\", config: { objects: [\"a\"] } }).success)\n      .toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// web/components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"@/components/severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"severity %i always renders its text label\", (sev) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={sev} />);\n    // guards the AGENTS.md rule: \"never render the mark without the word\"\n    expect(screen.getByText(SEVERITY_LABEL[sev])).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// web/components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders one row per source\", () => { ... });\n  it(\"joins multiple config.objects with a comma\", () => { ... });\n  it(\"renders an empty table body (not a crash) for an empty sources array\", () => {\n    // no explicit empty-state handling in this component today — worth\n    // deciding whether SourcesEmptyState is the caller's responsibility\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 11. Missing error-handling tests specifically\n\nNone of the above stub functions have any tests for their failure paths because none exist yet, but the following are the highest-value error cases to lock in once implemented:\n\n| Function | Missing failure-path test |\n|---|---|\n| `normalize()` | record missing `Id`/`Name`; unknown `entity_type` |\n| `SurvivorshipRule` | `prefer_source` without `preferred_source_id` (covered above) — also: unknown `strategy` literal |\n| `validate()` | value that's a *substring* of an observed value (must still fail unless it's a legal normalization) |\n| `main.execute_run()` | a pipeline stage raising mid-run → `runs.status` must land on `\"failed\"` with `error` populated, not hang in an intermediate status |\n| `db.write_*` | writing to a nonexistent `run_id` (FK violation) should surface, not silently no-op |\n| `requireReviewer()` | Clerk `auth()` throwing (network/config error) vs. simply unauthenticated — currently both paths look identical to the caller |\n| route handlers (once built) | every POST/PATCH in `web/app/api/` needs a \"Zod validation fails → 400, not 500\" test, per AGENTS.md's \"every route handler validates its body with Zod before touching the database. No exceptions.\" |\n\n---\n\n### 12. Integration test gaps\n\nThese don't exist because the pieces they'd connect aren't implemented, but they're the tests that matter most once Phase 2–4 land:\n\n1. **Full pipeline, synthetic seed → manifest**: `extract (SyntheticConnector) → normalize → block/match → detect → resolve`, asserting against `eval/generate.py`'s ground truth — this is `eval/harness.py`'s job and currently has no test of its own correctness.\n2. **`main.execute_run` end-to-end against a test Postgres**: run status transitions through every state in order (`queued → extracting → matching → detecting → resolving → complete`), never skipping a state, never regressing.\n3. **Web ⇄ engine contract round-trip**: a `StartRunRequest` built in `web/lib/server/engine.ts` (not yet written) serializes to exactly what `engine/pipeline/schema.py`'s `StartRunRequest` deserializes — a JSON fixture test on both sides guards the \"change both sides in the same commit\" rule mechanically instead of by discipline alone.\n4. **Table-ownership enforcement**: a test that runs a full engine execution against a scratch DB and asserts `sources` and `rulesets` rows are byte-identical before and after — the only thing currently stopping the engine from writing them is a docstring.\n5. **Ruleset versioning immutability**: POST to `/api/rulesets` (once built) creates a new row rather than mutating an existing `id` — no test exists because the route doesn't exist yet, but it's called out explicitly in AGENTS.md as a reproducibility requirement.\n6. **Auth-gated routes**: no test currently proves `proxy.ts`'s matcher and each route handler's `requireReviewer()` call actually agree — the code itself says \"should be covered by proxy.ts\" as an assumption, not a verified one.\n\n---\n\n**Bottom line**: this is a greenfield-coverage problem, not a regression-coverage problem. The two priorities I'd sequence first are (1) wiring up Vitest + pytest so any of the above can actually run, and (2) writing the `agent/graph.py` `validate()` and `should_auto_apply()` tests before implementing them, since AGENTS.md treats those two functions as the system's only non-negotiable safety property.\n",
